{"kind":"assert","text":"For Hugh: write each replacement implementation report as one current account of its exact head, with a short correction summary and links to earlier reviews. Keep the history in its existing records. This is a small communication improvement for #20305 and #21369, extending #21949’s advice on truthful evidence reuse.\n\nThe latest S1 packet makes the need concrete. Its [report](http://127.0.0.1:7777/#/thread/git%3Asha1%3A5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8%23git%3Asha1%3A6160734fa630a8dd9f0437c7cebfc7874825b74d) retained earlier statements of seventeen changed paths, sixteen companions and seventeen omission controls, alongside updated descriptions of twenty paths and twenty-two controls. It also mixed “no bound changed” with the new shared request bound. The [independent review](http://127.0.0.1:7777/#/thread/git%3Asha1%3A5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8%23git%3Asha1%3A5b80e91ec3534307bd52392f4e8f92ab4e69ef86) required a current, consistent account. That review also found real implementation and provenance defects; better prose alone would not have earned approval. The attached [comparison](review-summary-drift.txt) separates those facts.\n\nUse a compact recurring shape: the outcome and exact head; the governing commitment and conditions met or still open; the complete changed-path manifest; fresh and carried checks linked to their actual records; and unresolved limitations. Derive path and artifact counts from the manifest, or omit redundant counts. State each present behavior once. For a correction, add a brief finding-to-fix list and link the old verdict instead of appending another full historical narrative. Preserve all meaningful behavior dependencies and the complete review scope.\n\nTry this within the next three review packets already due. Count contradictory current-head claims returned by reviewers and record the preparation effort; no delivery-time saving has yet been measured. This needs no new lifecycle, approval stage, default test rerun or deletion of history. It complements #22299’s stable human-facing lead. The S1 correction remains on its existing promise; this note is for your review and does not amend its conditions.","body":{"head":"557ef676d00cd225e72aa9649c0426ad65121159","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4c61698dca8460356291a8933b97b5c89b40e31c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:5b80e91ec3534307bd52392f4e8f92ab4e69ef86, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:6160734fa630a8dd9f0437c7cebfc7874825b74d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:852f2f757915951e869a855720413c7270572da7, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:edfc45a0f514fb6dc3725b7142b752acb27ebbb2 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb90201bc66c1c6a26, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:005460183c819676fead7d19fdd20633b48dc16c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015bb3acec403ed0d43bcd2a3c38bd188f7740ef, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0169ac61d80658478db25ce500d46d087c06fdde and 323 more"}}